class.description:
A [FilesManifest] describes a set of files as data instead of code: folders (optionally with their subfolders), the extensions and the type of the files to take from them, and single files. Create it in the Inspector or in code, save it as a resource, and load everything it describes with [method ResourceLoader.load_manifest] or [method ResourceLoader.load_threaded_request_manifest]. [method ResourceLoader.get_manifest_paths] returns the paths without loading them.
Paths may use any prefix of [PathPrefixServer], for example [code]res://[/code], [code]user://[/code], [code]exec://[/code] or [code]appdata://[/code]. Relative paths are relative to [code]res://[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var manifest := FilesManifest.new()
manifest.type_hint = &"Texture2D"
manifest.extensions = PackedStringArray(["png", "webp"])
manifest.folder_paths = PackedStringArray(["res://art/icons", "res://art/portraits"])
var textures := ResourceLoader.load_manifest(manifest)
print(textures.size(), " textures loaded")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var manifest = new FilesManifest
{
    TypeHint = "Texture2D",
    Extensions = ["png", "webp"],
    FolderPaths = ["res://art/icons", "res://art/portraits"],
};
Godot.Collections.Dictionary textures = ResourceLoader.LoadManifest(manifest);
GD.Print(textures.Count, " textures loaded");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Folders are listed with [method ResourceLoader.list_directory], so imported files are found by their original names in the editor and in exported projects (files inside the PCK).
